  "notes": "New York's guitar-and-drum-machine soul miniaturist. `confidence` is **low** — the research rates the entry medium-low, sourcing the palette and the production scale but marking tempo and drum detail as inference. The drum block is the stated hybrid: \"a small, dry programmed kick and clap on 2&4 with quantised 16th hats, plus shaker, finger-snaps and tambourine played live over it\". The word *quantised* is why `quantizeStrength` sits at 0.88 with the snare exactly on the grid, and *played live over it* is why the percussion lanes run 4–7 hits a bar — the machine is rigid and the hands are not. Harmony is \"maj7/6-9 tonics, ii–V turnarounds, and chromatic bass motion under static top notes\", written on guitar so \"open strings and add9 shapes recur\", which is the ii–V family, `topVoiceStepwise` for the static top, and `susSubstitutionProb` for the add9s. Melody is \"light, breathy soprano at low volume, high syllabic density with small intervals, and heavily multi-tracked in close thirds on the hook\" — the high register, near-total stepwise motion, density 5–9 and an octave-echo counter for the multi-tracking. Bass is \"short and muted, root-and-fifth with 8th-note motion and occasional slides\", a kick mirror with a real glide. ⚠ Every drum, melody and bass number here is INFERRED. ⚠ Her ii–V family is shared with several other jazz-voiced models in this section because the research gives them the same turnaround; the separation is authored in the kit, the register and the density.",
